  partId: avionics
  displayName: Avionics and Flight Computers
  shortName: Avionics
  zone: 1
  order: 140
  keySpec: Redundant radiation-tolerant computers
  summary: "Orion's flight computers, navigation sensors and data networks. Beyond
    Earth's magnetic field there is no shielding from cosmic rays, and a single high-energy
    particle can flip a bit in memory \u2014 a single event upset."
  whyItMatters: 'The answer is redundancy and voting: several computers run the same
    calculation and compare answers, so a corrupted result is outvoted rather than
    acted on. The processors are deliberately generations behind consumer hardware,
    because larger transistors are far harder for a cosmic ray to disturb.'
  narration: {fileID: 0}
